  "configuration_id": "config_001",
  "reason": "With no prior evidence, the priority is to establish a clean multimodal baseline that is cheap and interpretable. config_001 (multimodal, singleprofile, pca_n2000, resnet50, concat) is the simplest full multimodal configuration: PCA is nearly free, ResNet50 is a moderate-cost CNN, singleprofile avoids aggregation overhead, and concat is trivial. This experiment tests whether a straightforward multimodal fusion of standard features achieves a competitive accuracy, giving us a floor to compare against more expensive encoders (scgpt, ViT-L), multiprofile aggregation, and alternative fusion strategies in subsequent runs. It is the best use of experiment 1 because it is low-cost (expected relative cost: low, roughly 1× a baseline run), preserves GPU budget for the 9 remaining experiments, and immediately tells us whether the multimodal signal is strong enough to justify investing in heavier encoders and aggregation in later trials."
}

